    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Fathom is a San Francisco-based company, founded in 2020 and publicly traded under the ticker FTHM, that offers an AI-powered meeting notetaker for Zoom, Google Meet, and Microsoft Teams calls. The company describes its core product as capturing, transcribing, and summarizing calls automatically, with the stated aim that users need never take notes manually. The product is offered free to individuals and includes AI-powered CRM update features for teams.\n\nThe Fathom product includes a conversational search interface called \"Ask Fathom,\" which the company describes as a place to search across meetings and retrieve customizable AI summaries tailored to a team's workflow. Additional features include AI Scorecards for real-time coaching and performance tracking, automated action items and call insights, and CRM integration that the company says updates records without manual input.\n\nThe held facts add that Fathom maintains a registered MCP server described as giving AI assistants real meeting context so outputs are grounded in a user's actual work. The company is registered with a CIK of 0001753162, confirming its public-company status, and no litigation has been recorded in the site's held facts.",
